select_CNN_training.mlapp
==========================

Purpose
-------
Wacom-friendly App Designer annotation tool for making 3-frame CNN/UNet
training samples from rectified wave video.

Inputs
------
1. Local waveIMG root directory.
2. Directory containing the new mp4/avi video(s).
3. Camera ID understood by define_camera_parameters_new(), e.g. top21,
   bot21, or rod13.

Pre-processing
--------------
The app follows the geometry and 3-frame stack logic in MAIN_FLOW_RECENT.m:
- VideoReader and info.freq determine the sampled frame sequence.
- Frames are converted to grayscale.
- Frames are rectified onto the X/Y grid using getUVfromXYZ().
- Three consecutive sampled frames are stored as RGB channels in IMG.
- Optional intensity enhancement is available.

Annotation classes
------------------
0   background / outside image
127 water
255 breaking wave / foam

The initial mask is background outside the valid rectified image and water
inside it. The annotator paints regions with a Wacom pen using the
Background, Water, and Breaking buttons. Undo/reset and an erase-to-water
tool are provided.

Archive
-------
Files are saved under:
  trainingData/trainingImages/<video>_Frame_<middle-frame>.png
  trainingData/trainingLabels/<video>_Frame_<middle-frame>.png
  trainingData/trainingMeta/<video>_Frame_<middle-frame>.mat

The .mat metadata includes the source video, 3 contributing video frame
indices, camera ID, X/Y coordinates, grid spacing, enhancement setting,
class definitions, and output filenames.

Important
---------
The app does not modify GitHub. It writes only to the selected local
waveIMG directory.

Compatibility note
------------------
The .mlapp was produced by replacing the source-code document inside the
existing App Designer package. The runtime class is self-contained, but the
App Designer design-time appModel is inherited from the older application.
If App Designer shows stale design-time component metadata, use the .m
source (select_CNN_training.m) as the authoritative editable source or
open and save the app in the target MATLAB release once.
